#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:154
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Quoted directly from the <filename>INSTALL</filename> file: <quote>Some of "
"the mimetype-related functionality in GIO requires the <command>update-mime-"
"database</command> and <command>update-desktop-database</command> "
"utilities,</quote> which are part of <xref role=\"runtime\" "
"linkend=\"shared-mime-info\"/> and <xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"desktop-"
"file-utils\"/>, respectively.  These two utilities are also needed for some "
"tests."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:167
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of GLib"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:170
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If desired, apply the optional patch. In many cases, applications that use "
"this library, either directly or indirectly via other libraries such as "
"<xref linkend=\"gtk3\"/>, output numerous warnings when run from the command"
" line.  This patch enables the use of an environment variable, "
"<envar>GLIB_LOG_LEVEL</envar>, that suppresses unwanted messages. The value "
"of the variable is a digit that corresponds to:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><simplelist><member>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:179
#, xml-text
msgid "1 Alert"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><simplelist><member>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:180
#, xml-text
msgid "2 Critical"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><simplelist><member>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:181
#, xml-text
msgid "3 Error"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><simplelist><member>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:182
#, xml-text
msgid "4 Warning"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><simplelist><member>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:183
#, xml-text
msgid "5 Notice"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:187
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For instance <userinput>export GLIB_LOG_LEVEL=4</userinput> will skip output"
" of Warning and Notice messages (and Info/Debug messages if they are turned "
"on).  If <envar>GLIB_LOG_LEVEL</envar> is not defined, normal message output"
" will not be affected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:193
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>patch -Np1 -i ../glib-skip_warnings-1.patch</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><warning><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:197
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If a previous version of glib is installed, move the headers out of the way "
"so that later packages do not encounter conflicts:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><warning><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:201
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"pre\">if [ -e /usr/include/glib-2.0 ]; then\n"
"    rm -rf /usr/include/glib-2.0.old &amp;&amp;\n"
"    mv -vf /usr/include/glib-2.0{,.old}\n"
"fi</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:215
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>GLib</application> by running the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:219
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup ..                  \\\n"
"      --prefix=/usr             \\\n"
"      --buildtype=release       \\\n"
"      -D introspection=disabled \\\n"
"      -D glib_debug=disabled    \\\n"
"      -D man-pages=enabled      \\\n"
"      -D sysprof=disabled       &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:232
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The <application>GLib</application> test suite requires "
"<application>desktop-file-utils</application> for some tests. However, "
"<application>desktop-file-utils</application> requires "
"<application>GLib</application> in order to compile; therefore, you must "
"first install <application>GLib</application> and then run the test suite."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:241
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"As the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user, install this "
"package for the first time to allow building GObject Introspection:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:246
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:315
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>ninja install</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:249
#, xml-text
msgid "Build GObject Introspection:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:252
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>tar xf ../../gobject-introspection-&gobject-introspection-version;.tar.xz &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup gobject-introspection-&gobject-introspection-version; gi-build \\\n"
"            --prefix=/usr --buildtype=release     &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja -C gi-build</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:259
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To test the results of GObject Introspection, issue: <command>ninja -C gi-"
"build test</command>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:264
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"As the &root; user, install GObject Introspection for generating the "
"introspection data of GLib libraries (required by various packages using "
"Glib, especially some GNOME packages):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:269
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>ninja -C gi-build install</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:272
#, xml-text
msgid "Now generate the introspection data:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:275
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>meson configure -D introspection=enabled &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:279
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you have <xref linkend='gi-docgen'/> installed and wish to build the API "
"documentation for this package, issue:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:283
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>sed \"/docs_dir =/s|$| / 'glib-' + meson.project_version()|\" \\\n"
"    -i ../docs/reference/meson.build                        &amp;&amp;\n"
"meson configure -D documentation=true                       &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><warning><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:290
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Do not run the test suite as &root; or some tests will fail unexpectedly and"
" leave some non-FHS-compliant directories in the <filename "
"class='directory'>/usr</filename> hierarchy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:298
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If the GLIB_LOG_LEVEL environment variable is set, unset it before running "
"the tests. Also one file that was created in the first install instruction "
"above needs to be writable.  As the &root; user, run <userinput>chmod a+rw "
".ninja_log</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:306
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To test the results, issue: <command>LC_ALL=C ninja test</command> as a "
"non-&root; user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:311
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"As the &root; user, install this package again for the introspection data "
"(and optionally, the documentation):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:320
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:326
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D man-pages=enabled</parameter>: This switch causes the build to"
" create and install the package man pages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:331
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D glib_debug=disabled</parameter>: This switch causes the build "
"to not include some expensive checks for debugging in the built programs and"
" libraries."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/genlib/glib2.xml:337
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D sysprof=disabled</parameter>: This switch disables the tracing"
" support for sysprof.  Remove this option if you want the tracing support.  "
"Note that if sysprof is not installed, removing this option will cause the "
"build system to download a copy of sysprof from the Internet."
msgstr ""

